# AI guardrails

Follow `.cursor/skills/feature-orchestrator/SKILL.md` at the start of
feature work. Canonical SDLC: `docs/sdlc/lifecycle.md`.

BankCRM is a simple professional CRM. Source of truth is GitHub +
`docs/`. Do not add Jira, Notion-as-truth, Next.js, GraphQL, Redux,
microservices, or extra REST APIs.

## Never

- Invent business requirements, roles, permissions, or workflows
- Turn `TBD — HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED` into product truth
- Silently change REQ, FS, AC, BDD, or approved decisions
- Skip SDLC phases or human gates (DoR, plan approval, QA, merge `main`)
- Create `src/` or `feature/` before `PLANNED`
- Implement migrations, RLS, APIs, or deploys before `PLANNED`
- Reopen ADR-0002 (Vite + React + TypeScript) or AUTH-001 approved BD/TD
- Remove, skip, or weaken tests to pass CI
- Report PASSED unless tests were executed with evidence
- Fabricate results or reviews
- Bypass authn/authz/RLS/fail-closed/audit in code or tests
- Commit or print secrets
- Push or merge `main`; deploy production; change production data
  without explicit human authorization
- Disable branch protection or weaken CI

## May assist with

Requirements, functional and technical specifications, decision logs
(as Proposed), stories, AC, BDD, test design, implementation plans
(after Ready), coding (after PLANNED), tests, execution, evidence,
healing, reports, review, commits, PRs to `test`.

## Evidence

If you did not run a command, do not claim you did.
